---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PromptList from '../components/PromptList.astro';
import prompts from '../data/prompts.json';

const count = prompts.filter((p) => p.tool === 'claude-code').length;
---

<Layout
  title={`Claude Code Prompts: ${count}+ Copy-Ready Prompts & Workflows (2026) | VibePrompt`}
  description="Copy-ready Claude Code prompts: systematic debugging workflows, root-cause analysis, SaaS MVP scaffolding with Next.js + Supabase + Stripe, schema design and launch hardening. Paste into Claude Code and go."
>
  <nav class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4"><a href="/" class="hover:text-foreground">Home</a> / Claude Code Prompts</nav>
  <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Claude Code Prompts</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4 max-w-3xl">
    Claude Code is the most powerful agentic coding tool of 2026 — but most people still prompt it like a chatbot. The prompts below treat Claude Code as a
    <strong>junior pair with a senior's knowledge</strong>: contracts that stop it from patching before understanding, scaffolds that produce runnable SaaS skeletons in one shot,
    and debugging workflows that isolate root causes instead of guessing. Every prompt is copy-ready: open it, paste it, replace the angle-bracket placeholders.
  </p>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl">
    Start with the scene pages if you know what you're doing here:
    <a href="/claude-code/debugging-prompts/" class="text-primary hover:underline">debugging prompts</a> for bugs,
    <a href="/claude-code/saas-mvp-prompts/" class="text-primary hover:underline">SaaS MVP prompts</a> for building,
    <a href="/claude-code/code-review-prompts/" class="text-primary hover:underline">code review prompts</a> before you merge.
    New prompts are added every week.
  </p>
  <PromptList filter={(p) => p.tool === 'claude-code'} />
</Layout>
